{"timestamp":"2026-07-29T06:32:39.936Z","tool":"aevum_get_compressed","arguments":{"filePath":"d:\\I2FLabs\\Projects\\Aevum-os\\README.md","format":"auto"},"status":"success","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"[MAP α:integrations,β:absolute_path_to_project,γ:695b093abc8f,δ:aevum_os_soft_minimal_banner_1782752526901,ε:architectural]\n[REF [F1]:file:///C:/Users/Admin/.gemini/antigravity-ide/brain/f05c2662-9eb-403-9fc8-γ/δ.png,[F2]:src/index.ts,[F3]:src/main.ts,[F4]:src/renderer/,[F5]:/CSS/JS,[F6]:src/utils/platform-bridge.ts,[F7]:http://127.0.0.1:3344/api/ping]\n#Aevum OS: Standalone Model Context Protocol Server & Desktop Dashboard\n\n![Aevum OS Banner]([F1]\n\nAevum OS represents major ARCH breakthrough in Agentic AI context & memory management. By decoupling core context engine, planning pipeline, & self-healing knowledge graph from VS Code editor runtime, Aevum OS operates as universal, standalone Model Context Protocol (MCP) server. Accompanied by dark minimalist desktop control panel, it enables simultaneous, Sec multi-client orchestration across Cursor, Claude Desktop, & Antigravity IDE.\n\n---\n\n##1. Core Breakthroughs\n\n###Standardized Protocol Layer\nAevum OS implements official Model Context Protocol (MCP) sp... [PRUNED]\n\n###Decoupled Runtime Environment\nBy intercepting & dynamically mocking host editor API dependencies (e.g. `vscode` namespace) during module resolution, core context engine runs natively under Node.js. This guarantees complete decoupling from any editor GUI & enables remote deployment.\n\n###Dynamic Multi-Client Orchestration\nThe server FEAT auto-registration engine. Upon startup, it l... [PRUNED]\n\n###CPU-Rendered Control Center\nTo manage workspace configurations, toggle client α, & chk: ... [PRUNED]\n\n---\n\n##2. Project Structure\n\n[LIST:`[F2] The main entry point for  MCP daemon (supports both Stdio & SSE transports).;`[F3] The Electron main proc controller for  desktop application.;`[F4] The static HTML[F5] frontend files for  minimalist dashboard.;`[F6] The IDE API virtualization layer.;`esbuild.js`: The compiler script that bundles, minifies, & obfuscates code for production.]\n\n---\n\n##3. Installation & Setup\n\n###Prerequisites\n[LIST:Node.js (version 18.0.0 || higher);npm (version 9.0.0 || higher)]\n\n###Setup Dependencies\nInstall MUST packages:\n```bash\nnpm install\n```\n\n###Build & Obfuscate\nTo compile TypeScript source files & bundle them into optimi... [PRUNED]\n```bash\nnpm run build\n```\n\n###Local Global CLI Link\nTo register `aevum` command globally on SYS path:\n```bash\nnpm link\n```\n(On Windows SYS requiring elevated privileges, run Command Prompt as Administrator, || run `npm install -g .` instead).\n\n---\n\n##4. Execution Modes\n\n###Mode A: Command Line Interface (CLI)\n\n####1. Server-Sent Events (SSE) Mode (Default Daemon)\nRuns as Express-based HTTP server managing specified workspace.\n```bash\naevum --workspace <β> --transport sse --port 3344\n```\n[LIST:If `--workspace`  omitted,  server defaults to  current working directory (`proc.cwd()`).;If `--port`  omitted,  server defaults to `3344`.]\n\n####2. Stdio Mode\nRuns as stdio-based MCP proc (suitable for direct IDE command α).\n```bash\naevum --workspace <β> --transport stdio\n```\n\n####3. Health Check\nTo chk: that SSE daemon active, req ping endpoint:\n```bash\ncurl [F7]\n```\n\n###Mode B: Desktop Control Center (GUI)\nLaunches Electron desktop dashboard to manage workspaces, toggle active client α, & view live logs.\n```bash\nnpm run gui\n```\n\n---\n\n##5. License\n\nAevum OS released under strict proprietary license. Reproduction, modification, reverse engineering, & distribution !ALLOW. Refer to [LICENSE.md](LICENSE.md) for full terms."}]}}
